    urma: fix bond jetty shared jfc refcount
    
    When a share_jfr jetty is created without an explicit shared.jfc, the core layer fills the effective recv JFC from shared.jfr->jfr_cfg.jfc. The bonding create path must take the same effective JFC reference that the delete path later releases; otherwise repeated create/delete flows can underflow the shared JFC use count and block cleanup.
    
    Take the JFC reference from the effective jetty config after create succeeds, avoid NULL replacement JFC layout assumptions in the pjetty path, and cover the issue cleanup order with regression tests. Also keep the JFCE device-name copy from truncating overlong sysfs names so warning-as-error builds pass.
    
    Signed-off-by: luyizhou <luyizhou1@huawei.com>

