    In bonding interrupt mode, epoll can report a physical JFCE whose provider wait returns no completion. The old path returned 0 once all reported physical events were empty, which can make callers miss a later backup completion after a stale primary event.
    
    Scan all reported physical JFCE events while capping returned virtual JFCs to the caller supplied count. Keep zero-timeout polling nonblocking, bound finite waits by an absolute monotonic deadline, and add a short backoff when readable physical events still have no completion.
    
    Add regression coverage for stale physical events, backup event scanning, infinite waits, and finite timeout retry behavior.
    
    Signed-off-by: luyizhou <luyizhou1@huawei.com>

