    ums: fix timing of CLC session registration and token value operations in token exchange
    
    Description:
    Fix the ordering of multiple operations in the token exchange flow
    to eliminate race conditions and ensure correct token values at each
    stage.
    
    Timing fixes:
    1. Register CLC session BEFORE handshake (connect/listen), so token
       delivery callbacks can always find the session.
    2. Assign local tokens (jetty_token, seg_token) to token_ctx AFTER
       buffer registration but BEFORE submitting to agent.
    3. Apply peer jetty token to link AFTER token exchange completes via
       ums_link_update_peer_jetty_token, instead of prematurely in
       ums_link_save_peer_info.
    4. Move memzero_explicit for token secrets BEFORE error checks to
       ensure cleanup on failure paths.
    
    Structural refactoring to enable the above:
    * Extract ums_token_xchg_ctx from ums_connection to decouple netlink
      callbacks from the connection object, enabling earlier registration.
    * Split ums_nl_register_and_submit_tokens into separate register and
      submit functions.
    
    Additional changes:
    * Guard idle timeout check with UMS_AGENT_ENABLE_IDLE_TIMEOUT_CHECK,
      set ever_used in send/recv instead of pool_get.
    * Remove handshake_complete_time, use last_active_time for idle
      timeout.
    * Change token log levels from INFO to DEBUG in ums_agent_nl.

