    ﻿ums: implement secure UB token exchange via ums_agent
    
    Description:
    Replace the boolean ub_token_disable with a three-mode ub_token_mode
    system (SECURE/LEGACY/DISABLE) and implement out-of-band token
    exchange via ums_agent in SECURE mode. In SECURE mode, UB tokens
    are delivered through ums_agent TLS channel instead of being sent
    as plaintext in CLC messages, preventing token leakage on the wire.
    1. Add clc_session_id to CLC handshake for correlating netlink
       token exchange with CLC sessions.
    2. Add ub_token_mode field in CLC accept/confirm messages and
       validate mode match on both client and server.
    3. Securely clear token values with memzero_explicit after use.
    4. Add configurable ums_agent_uid/gid module parameters with
       auto-learn and strict verification modes.
    5. Fix ums_agent_nl error handling for -NLE_INTR and reconnect.
    
    Key changes:
    * ums_clc.c: add clc_session_id, token mode switch, clear tokens
    * ums_clc.h: add clc_session_id, ub_token_mode bitfield, decline codes
    * ums_core.c: token exchange wait/complete, session id generation,
      nl_refcnt lifecycle
    * ums_nl.c: remove token debug logs, add UMS_IPV6_ADDR_LEN
    * ums_ubcore.c: use ub_token_mode enum, clear token values
    * ums_wr.c: use ub_token_mode enum instead of boolean
    * ums_connect.c: register/submit tokens, wait for exchange,
      validate peer mode
    * ums_listen.c: register/submit tokens, validate peer mode,
      unregister on error
    * ums_mod.c: add ub_token_mode param, deprecate ub_token_disable,
      add ums_agent_uid/gid params, init nl
    * ums_common.c: use saved token in SECURE mode for jetty import
    * ums_types.h: remove ub_token_disable field
    * ums_agent_nl.c: fix -NLE_INTR handling and reconnect logic

